    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d315">

                <pb facs="0444" n="362" xml:id="pg362"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89 Italy/48</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Blair &amp; Co.,
                        Incorporated</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-09-01"><hi rendition="#italic">September 1,
                        1925</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In confirmation of Mr. Young’s<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d315-f1"/> statement to Mr. Sheldon<anchor n="5" xml:id="d315-f2"/>
                    on August 31, in response to Mr. Sheldon’s inquiry concerning the attitude of
                    the Department of State in regard to the flotation of Italian industrial
                    securities in the United States, I beg to say that this Department would not
                    view such financing with favor at the present time.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph C. Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
